From 9d8660d3f67a559c2772edce82e3b7ef28275207 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Axel Tobieson <axel.tobieson@spiideo.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 22:37:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat: export per-macroblock H.264 analysis as AVFrame
 side data

Adds AV_FRAME_DATA_SL_H264_ANALYSIS: a packed blob of per-MB records
attached to every decoded AVFrame when the h264 decoder option
"export_sl_analysis" is set to 1.

Layout (libavutil/sl_h264_analysis.h):
  SLH264AnalysisHeader   (version=1, mb_width, mb_height, mb_stride)
  SLH264MBRecord[mb_width * mb_height]  (raster order, row-major)

Per-MB record fields:
  mb_type        - raw FFmpeg MB_TYPE_* flags (mpegutils.h semantics)
  sub_mb_type[4] - sub-MB partition types per 8x8 block
  mv[2][16][2]   - quarter-pel MVs per list per 4x4 block (b_stride layout)
  ref_idx[2][4]  - reference index per list per 8x8 partition, -1=unused
  intra4x4_pred_modes[16] - scan4 order; FFmpeg internal modes 0-11
                            (0-8 standard H.264, 9-11 DC edge variants);
                            0x7F when not an INTRA4x4 MB
  chroma_pred_mode    - FFmpeg 8x8 chroma pred mode (0-3 standard, 4-9
                        internal DC edge variants); 0xFF for inter MBs
  intra16x16_pred_mode - same scale as chroma; 0xFF when not INTRA16x16
  transform_8x8  - 1 if MB_TYPE_8x8DCT
  qp             - luma quantization parameter for this MB
  slice_id       - h->slice_table[mb_xy], or 0xFFFF if unavailable

Implementation notes:
- Side data blob is allocated on pic->f at frame start (h264_frame_start)
  and filled per-MB in ff_h264_hl_decode_mb immediately after entropy
  decoding. It travels with the picture through the DPB, so B-frame
  display reordering is transparent.
- Intra prediction modes are captured from sl->intra4x4_pred_mode_cache
  (post write_back, post check_intra4x4_pred_mode), giving the actual
  modes used for reconstruction including FFmpeg's edge-case DC variants.
- Chroma/16x16 modes from sl->chroma_pred_mode / sl->intra16x16_pred_mode.
- MVs and ref indices from h->cur_pic.motion_val / h->cur_pic.ref_index,
  populated by write_back_motion before ff_h264_hl_decode_mb is called.
- Sub-MB types from sl->sub_mb_type (uint16_t[4], widened to uint32_t).
- REQUIRES threads=1. Frame threading is incompatible; set
  avctx->thread_count = 1 before avcodec_open2.
- AV_FRAME_DATA_SL_H264_ANALYSIS appended at end of AVFrameSideDataType
  enum (additive; ABI drift vs system ffmpeg acceptable for vendored build).

Fields omitted (would require deep surgery):
- cbp: available in h->cbp_table but not per-picture persistent; deferred.
- Per-MB bit counts: explicitly out of scope (phase 2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
